-- title:
--   Theorem 3.3(3), p. 7 — exit from (a, b): (3.8) expectation of f(X_T), (3.9) density of G^(a,b)∁, (3.10) ℙ_x(T_(a,b)∁ < ζ) (part 3 of 4; companions theorem_3_3_1, _2, _4)
-- statement:
--   Let $E=[\mathfrak l,\mathfrak h]\cap\mathbb Z$ and let $(X,\mathbb P)$ be the Markov chain with state space $E$ generated by a Q-matrix $Q$ (not necessarily conservative) that is skip-free downward, i.e. satisfies (2.1): $Q(x,x-1)>0$ for $x>\mathfrak l$ and $Q(x,y)=0$ for $y\le x-2$. Assume all states are transient and fix a reference point $\mathfrak o\in E$. Write $G$ for the resolvent, $\zeta$ for the lifetime and $T_A$ for the first hitting time of $A$. Let $H$, $\widehat H$, $\mathbf H^{[b}$ and $\mathfrak C$ be as in Theorem 3.1. Let $\pi$ be the positive excessive reference measure.
--
--   Let $a<b$ in $E$, so that $E^{(a,b)^\complement}=E\cap(a,b)=\{a+1,\dots,b-1\}$, let $T=T_{(a,b)^\complement}$ be the exit time from $(a,b)$ and $G^{(a,b)^\complement}$ the resolvent of the chain killed at $T$ (extended by $0$), with density $\mathfrak g^{(a,b)^\complement}(x,y)=G^{(a,b)^\complement}(x,y)/\pi(y)$. Then:
--
--   1. for every $f:E\to\mathbb R$ with $Q|f|(x)=\sum_yQ(x,y)|f(y)|<\infty$ for all $x\in E^{(a,b)^\complement}$, and every $x\in E$,
--   $$\mathbb E_x\big[f(X_T)\mathbb 1_{\{T<\zeta\}}\big]=f(x)+\sum_{z\in E^{(a,b)^\complement}}Qf(z)\,G^{(a,b)^\complement}(x,z),\qquad Qf(z)=\sum_{y\in E}Q(z,y)f(y);\tag{3.8}$$
--   2. for $x,y\in E^{(a,b)^\complement}$,
--   $$\mathfrak g^{(a,b)^\complement}(x,y)=\mathfrak C\,\widehat H(y)\Big(\frac{\mathbf H^{[b}(x)}{\mathbf H^{[b}(a)}\mathbf H^{[y}(a)-\mathbf H^{[y}(x)\Big);\tag{3.9}$$
--   3. for $x\in E$,
--   $$\mathbb P_x\big(T<\zeta\big)=1-\sum_{z\in E^{(a,b)^\complement}}Q(z,\partial)\,G^{(a,b)^\complement}(x,z).\tag{3.10}$$
--
--   These identities describe the exit from a finite interval, including the law of the exit position.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: E = [𝔩, 𝔥] ∩ ℤ with 𝔩 < 𝔥 in ℤ ∪ {±∞} → E : Set ℤ with E.OrdConnected and two points x < y in E (𝔩 = −∞ iff ¬ BddBelow E, 𝔥 = ∞ iff ¬ BddAbove E); reason: an order-connected subset of ℤ with at least two points is exactly such an integer interval
--   - encoding: all states in E are transient → AllTransient E Q: G(x, x) < ∞ for every x ∈ E; reason: Norris, Markov Chains, Theorem 3.4.2, which the paper itself invokes on p. 3; an absorbing state has G(x, x) = ∞
--   - encoding: the Markov chain (X, ℙ) generated by Q (jump chain/holding time definition, p. 2) → transition, resolvent, hitProb, hitBeforeProb, exitDist, killedResolvent computed from jump-chain path sums with Exp(1) holding clocks; reason: this is the paper's construction (i)–(iv); the cemetery ∂ is represented by leaving E
--   - encoding: the fixed positive excessive reference measure π of p. 3 (standing for Section 3) → explicit hypotheses π : ℤ → ℝ, ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x, IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π; reason: the section's standing assumption written into the binders
--   - encoding: real-valued probabilities ℙ_x(…) → ℝ≥0∞-valued path sums compared through .toReal; reason: a probability is at most 1, so .toReal loses nothing
--   - encoding: f : E → ℝ → f : ℤ → ℝ, only its values on E are used; reason: same instances
--   - encoding: Q|f|(x) < ∞ for x ∈ E^{(a,b)∁} → Summable (y ↦ |Q(x, y)| |f(y)|) over y ∈ E, for x ∈ (a, b); reason: only the diagonal entry of Q is negative, so the two conditions coincide
--   - encoding: 𝔼_x[f(X_T) 1_{T<ζ}] → HasSum over z ∈ E of f(z) · ℙ_x(X_T = z, T < ζ); reason: the expectation of a function of the exit position, summed over its law; HasSum over a countable type in ℝ is absolute convergence, which the expectation presupposes
--   - encoding: sums over z ∈ E^{(a,b)∁} → Finset.Ioo a b; reason: E is an interval containing a and b, so E ∩ (a, b) = (a, b) ∩ ℤ
--   - encoding: G^{(a,b)∁}(x, z) as a real number → conclusion clause killedResolvent … ≠ ⊤, then .toReal; reason: G^{(a,b)∁} ≤ G < ∞ (p. 3); the clause makes .toReal faithful
--   - reading: the notation of Theorem 3.1: H(x), H^{[y}(x) = lim_{y↓𝔩} …, Ĥ(y) = lim_{x↑𝔥} … (no printed case split for H^{[b} and Ĥ) → fundH, fundHb, fundHhat: value at 𝔩 (resp. 𝔥) when E is bounded below (resp. above), limUnder along atBot (resp. atTop) otherwise; existence of these limits is asserted in theorem_3_1_1 and theorem_3_1_3; reason: the paper defines the notation lim_{y↓𝔩} by this case split for H in Theorem 3.1(1); Theorem 3.3 is stated 'using its notation'
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, p. 7, Theorem 3.3(3), (3.8)–(3.10)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Chain
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-- Theorem 3.3(3), p. 7, (3.8)–(3.10). Under the assumptions of Theorem 3.1 (with the positive
excessive reference measure `π`), let `a < b` in `E`, so that `E^{(a,b)∁} = E ∩ (a, b)` is the
finite set `{a + 1, …, b - 1}`. For every `f : E → ℝ` with `Q|f|(x) < ∞` on `E^{(a,b)∁}` and every
`x ∈ E`:
(3.8) `𝔼_x[f(X_{T_{(a,b)∁}}) 1_{T_{(a,b)∁} < ζ}] = f(x) + ∑_{z ∈ E^{(a,b)∁}} Qf(z) G^{(a,b)∁}(x, z)`;
(3.9) `𝔤^{(a,b)∁}(x, y) = ℭ Ĥ(y) (H^{[b}(x)/H^{[b}(a) · H^{[y}(a) - H^{[y}(x))` for
`x, y ∈ E^{(a,b)∁}`;
(3.10) `ℙ_x(T_{(a,b)∁} < ζ) = 1 - ∑_{z ∈ E^{(a,b)∁}} Q(z, ∂) G^{(a,b)∁}(x, z)`. -/
theorem theorem_3_3_3 (E : Set ℤ) (Q : ℤ → ℤ → ℝ) (hE : IsStateSpace E) (hQ : IsQMatrix E Q)
    (hS : SkipFreeDown E Q) (hT : AllTransient E Q) (o : ℤ) (ho : o ∈ E)
    (π : ℤ → ℝ) (hπpos : ∀ x ∈ E, 0 < π x) (hπ : IsExcessiveMeasure E Q π)
    (a b : ℤ) (ha : a ∈ E) (hb : b ∈ E) (hab : a < b) :
    (∀ x z : ℤ, killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x z ≠ ⊤) ∧
    (∀ f : ℤ → ℝ, (∀ x ∈ Set.Ioo a b, Summable (fun y : E => |Q x y| * |f y|)) →
      ∀ x ∈ E,
        HasSum (fun z : E => f z * (exitDist E Q (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x z).toReal)
          (f x + ∑ z ∈ Finset.Ioo a b,
            (∑' y : E, Q z y * f y) * (killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x z).toReal)) ∧
    (∀ x ∈ Set.Ioo a b, ∀ y ∈ Set.Ioo a b,
      killedRdens E Q π (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x y =
        rdens E Q π o o * fundHhat E Q π o y *
          (fundHb E Q o b x / fundHb E Q o b a * fundHb E Q o y a - fundHb E Q o y x)) ∧
    ∀ x ∈ E,
      (hitProb E Q (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x).toReal =
        1 - ∑ z ∈ Finset.Ioo a b,
          killRate E Q z * (killedResolvent E Q (Set.Ioo a b)ᶜ x z).toReal := by sorry

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI
